# Prohibited AI / tool / model / automated-service attribution identities
# for GNOVI Studio, used by githooks/authorship-check.sh.
#
# This is NOT a contributor allowlist. Ordinary human contributors --
# known or unknown -- are welcome and are never rejected merely for being
# unrecognized. A commit is rejected only if one of its identities
# (Author, Committer, or any "...-by" trailer such as Co-authored-by)
# exactly matches an entry below.
#
# Two matching modes, one identity per line:
#
#   * A line containing "<...>" is matched as an EXACT "Name <email>"
#     string against the full identity.
#   * A line with no "<...>" is matched, case-insensitively, as an EXACT
#     whole Name -- never a substring -- against the *name* part only of
#     an identity.
#
# Deliberately NOT included: bare model/company names ("Claude", "Gemini",
# "OpenAI", "Anthropic", "Google", ...) or email-domain patterns
# (e.g. "*@anthropic.com"). Those can be genuine human names, or genuine
# human contributors employed by those companies -- see
# githooks/README.md. Only identities that are themselves the name of an
# AI/tool/service, never a plausible human name, belong here.
#
# To add a newly-observed AI/tool identity, append it here in an ordinary
# reviewed commit.

Claude Code
